        "mode": "learn",
        "intro": "🙏 Before you begin: bathe and wear clean puja clothes that are used only for puja.\n\nPut a tilak on your own forehead. Tie a mukhkosh — a folded cloth over your nose and mouth — so your breath does not touch Bhagwan.\n\nChandan puja comes after jal puja (prakshal) and gently drying Bhagwan with soft cloths. Take chandan mixed with kesar in a clean bowl and use the ring finger (anamika) of your right hand. Never let your nail touch the murti.\n\nGo in this order: big toes, knees, wrists, shoulders, top of the head, forehead, throat, heart, navel — nine pujas, thirteen touches. For each pair, Bhagwan's right first, then his left. (Bhagwan faces you, so his right hand is on your left.)\n\nMany people recite a short doha at each place — your Pathshala teacher can teach them. Until then, some families say one line of the Navkar at each of the nine places, from “Namo Arihantanam” at the toes to “Padhamam Havai Mangalam” at the navel.",
