 ],
 "notes": "DRAFT for Pathshala review — every step activity and every quiz question carries review = \"needs_pathshala_review\". All explanations are written in our own words; no stavan/doha text is included.\n\nSutra text policy: the full Navkar Mantra is given in Devanagari in the Shvetambar Murtipujak reading (नमो, नमुक्कारो, हवइ), checked against two independent web sources plus the JAINA Education books (JES 931, JES 933) and the JCNC Samayik booklet. The spec example used the Digambar spelling णमो; we deliberately use नमो (hi-IN speech recognition also handles it better). For every other sutra only the first line is given, in Roman transliteration (checked against JES 931 and the JCNC booklet); the Khamasamana sutra is a single sentence and is given whole.\n\nSamayik vidhi follows the common Tapagachha-style sequence used by Gujarati Shvetambar Murtipujak families. Details differ between books and gachchhs: some start with three khamasamanas before the sthapana (the JCNC booklet does); some books show one khamasamana before a pair of requests rather than before each one. JSH Pathshala should confirm its own sequence. The 50 bol of muhapatti padilehan are deliberately not included — the teacher teaches them.\n\nPoints follow the spec table: read 5, quiz 10, practice 10, hotspot learn 10, hotspot practice 10 + repeat 3, voice 15 + repeat 3, level points 20. treasure_points 50 on Samayik levels 4 and 8. We ALSO set 50 on Navkar level 5 (Panch Parameshthi badge) because the table says \"badge levels\"; set it to 0 if only the two Samayik levels were meant. Navang puja level: treasure 0.\n\nPractice steps (kind \"practice\") have no payload in the 0570 contract, so we used the read-card shape: { cards: [...], confirm_label: \"I did it…\" } — the app can show the cards and a done button. \"Order\" activities are quiz questions of type \"order\". Quiz steps carry activity = { review } only. Choice answers are spread across positions (the app does not shuffle choice options).\n\nNavang puja hotspot: nine pujas but THIRTEEN touches (toes, knees, wrists and shoulders are pairs, right then left of the murti, as JAINA JES 933 and Jain Samaj of Long Island state). Each spot has an extra optional field \"puja\" (1–9) so the app can show \"puja 3 of 9\"; drop it if unwanted. If the app should treat each pair as one tap, merge pairs (keep 9 spots).\n\nCoordinates are for a placeholder seated padmasana, front-facing murti in a portrait 3:4 frame (x of width, y of height, r of width): head top y 0.08, navel 0.62, knees/toes ~0.86–0.89. Bhagwan faces the viewer, so his right shoulder/knee/wrist are on the viewer's LEFT. In padmasana each foot rests on the opposite thigh, so his RIGHT big toe is placed on the viewer's RIGHT (near his left knee). Some teachers instead teach \"start with the toe on Bhagwan's right side\" — CONFIRM WITH PATHSHALA and swap toe_right/toe_left x if needed. Re-place all spots on the real derasar photo.\n\nKnee meaning: some sources say Bhagwan reached kevalgyan \"standing\"; Shvetambar accounts place Mahavir Swami's kevalgyan in a squatting (godohika) posture, so the knee \"why\" only says he stood long in kayotsarg on his way to kevalgyan. Teacher to confirm wording.\n\nMukhkosh: we say \"a folded cloth over your nose and mouth\"; many families use an eight-fold cloth, but we could not confirm that number from two sources, so it is left out. The chandan doha for each place is not quoted; each \"why\" paraphrases the commonly taught meaning.\n\nDigambar practice differs: there is no Shvetambar-style nine-limb chandan puja on the murti (offerings are made in front of the murti, and practice varies between Digambar groups). Sthanakvasi and Terapanthi Shvetambars do not do murti puja. This module is for Shvetambar Murtipujak families only.\n\nSuggested metadata for the new goal (not binding): description, sort_order 50, tint #1F7A4D, mark \"Pu\", recommended false. Level chapter \"Chapter 1 · Chandan puja\".\n\nStories used: Puniya Shravak (Samayik level 1) and the yugalik coronation (toes \"why\"). Both are told gently; the \"hell\" detail of King Shrenik's story is softened to \"a hard future his past karma had made\"."
}
$gyan_pack_0571$::jsonb
$gyan_pack_fn$;

-- The fixed id of a pack step.
create or replace function app.gyan_pack_step_id(p_goal text, p_level text, p_position integer) returns uuid
language sql immutable set search_path = app, public, extensions as $$
  select md5('gyan_pack_0571:' || p_goal || ':' || p_level || ':' || p_position)::uuid
$$;

create or replace function app.apply_gyan_content_pack() returns jsonb
language plpgsql security definer set search_path = app, public, extensions as $$
declare
  v_pack jsonb := app.gyan_content_pack();
  g jsonb; l jsonb; s jsonb; v_lord bigint; v_sord bigint;
  v_goal uuid; v_level uuid; v_tp int;
  n_goals int := 0; n_levels int := 0; n_steps int := 0; n_treasure int := 0; v_missing text[] := '{}';
begin
  perform set_config('app.audit_reason', 'Gyan Path content pack (0571)', true);
  for g in select x from jsonb_array_elements(v_pack->'goals') x loop
    v_goal := null;
    select id into v_goal from app.gyan_goals where center_id is null and key = g->>'goal_key' order by sort_order, id limit 1;
    if v_goal is null then
      if not coalesce((g->>'new')::boolean, false) then
        v_missing := v_missing || (g->>'goal_key');
        continue;
      end if;
      insert into app.gyan_goals (center_id, tradition, key, name, description, sort_order, tint, mark, recommended)
        values (null, (g->>'tradition')::app.tradition, g->>'goal_key', g->>'goal_name', g->>'description',
                coalesce((g->>'sort_order')::int, 0), g->>'tint', g->>'mark', coalesce((g->>'recommended')::boolean, false))
        returning id into v_goal;
      n_goals := n_goals + 1;
    end if;

    for l, v_lord in select x, o from jsonb_array_elements(g->'levels') with ordinality as t(x, o) loop
      v_level := null;
      select id into v_level from app.gyan_levels where goal_id = v_goal and key = l->>'level_key';
      if v_level is null then
        select id into v_level from app.gyan_levels where goal_id = v_goal and lower(btrim(name)) = lower(btrim(l->>'level_name'))
         order by sort_order, id limit 1;
      end if;
      v_tp := coalesce((l->>'treasure_points')::int, 0);
      if v_level is null then
        insert into app.gyan_levels (goal_id, key, name, sort_order, points, chapter, treasure, treasure_points, requires_teacher_signoff)
          values (v_goal, l->>'level_key', l->>'level_name', coalesce((l->>'sort_order')::int, v_lord::int), coalesce((l->>'points')::int, 20),
                  l->>'chapter', l->>'treasure', v_tp, coalesce((l->>'requires_teacher_signoff')::boolean, false))
          returning id into v_level;
        n_levels := n_levels + 1;
      elsif v_tp > 0 then
        update app.gyan_levels set treasure_points = v_tp where id = v_level and treasure_points = 0;
        if found then n_treasure := n_treasure + 1; end if;
      end if;

      for s, v_sord in select x, o from jsonb_array_elements(l->'steps') with ordinality as t(x, o) loop
        insert into app.gyan_steps (id, level_id, kind, title, sort_order, points, repeat_points, activity, quiz)
          values (app.gyan_pack_step_id(g->>'goal_key', l->>'level_key', v_sord::int), v_level, s->>'kind', s->>'title', v_sord::int,
                  coalesce((s->>'points')::int, 0), coalesce((s->>'repeat_points')::int, 0), coalesce(s->'activity', '{}'::jsonb),
                  case when jsonb_typeof(s->'quiz') = 'object' then s->'quiz' end)
          on conflict (id) do nothing;
        if found then n_steps := n_steps + 1; end if;
      end loop;
    end loop;
  end loop;
  return jsonb_build_object('goals_added', n_goals, 'levels_added', n_levels, 'steps_added', n_steps,
                            'treasure_points_set', n_treasure, 'goals_not_here_yet', to_jsonb(v_missing));
end $$;

comment on function app.gyan_content_pack() is
  'The Gyan Path content pack of 0571 (goals, levels, steps, sources, notes), as built by supabase/scripts/build-gyan-pack.mjs.';
comment on function app.apply_gyan_content_pack() is
  'Platform only: put the 0571 content pack into the shared library. Idempotent; never changes or deletes a step it did not add, never overwrites a level''s treasure points. Returns what it added. seed.sql calls it again on a new database.';

revoke execute on function app.gyan_content_pack(), app.gyan_pack_step_id(text, text, integer), app.apply_gyan_content_pack()
  from public, anon, authenticated;
grant execute on function app.gyan_content_pack(), app.gyan_pack_step_id(text, text, integer), app.apply_gyan_content_pack() to service_role;

select app.apply_gyan_content_pack();
